{"operations":[{"content":"def median(data):\n    \"\"\"Return the median of the data.\n\n    For an even number of values, the median is the arithmetic mean of the two middle values (as a float).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        raise ValueError(\"median() arg is an empty sequence\")\n    sorted_data = sorted(data)\n    n = len(sorted_data)\n    mid = n // 2\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return float(sorted_data[mid])\n    else:\n        return (float(sorted_data[mid - 1]) + float(sorted_data[mid])) / 2.0\n","expected_sha256":"3a53872cc6d7b6454ddacc71bd93b27bda982c5d77ca27564a8fb3154fc82ae3","kind":"modify","path":"src/stats.py"}],"rationale":"Ensure the median for even-length data is always a float by converting the two middle values to float before averaging, fixing the defect while keeping the public API and existing tests intact."}